From: Olexandr Tyshchenko <o.tyshchenko@eslua.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: rockchip_dw_mmc: double the ciu clock for the card rate

On RK3288 and later SoCs the dw_mmc card interface clock comes from a
clock generator that divides the ciu clock by 2 (Linux:
RK3288_CLKGEN_DIV in dw_mmc-rockchip.c). U-Boot set the ciu clock to
the card rate and put the dw_mmc divider in bypass, so a high speed SD
card reported at 50 MHz ran at 25 MHz: about 12 MB/s on RK3566.

Ask the clock driver for twice the card rate; if it cannot provide it
(the 400 kHz identification clock on RK3568), keep the old behaviour.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
---
--- a/drivers/mmc/rockchip_dw_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/rockchip_dw_mmc.c
@@ -48,6 +48,18 @@
 	if (host->mmc->selected_mode == MMC_DDR_52 && host->mmc->bus_width == 8)
 		freq *= 2;
 
+	/*
+	 * The clock generator in front of the card interface divides the
+	 * ciu clock by 2 (RK3288_CLKGEN_DIV in Linux), so ask for twice the
+	 * rate and report the card rate: the dw_mmc divider stays in bypass.
+	 * Without this a "50 MHz" high speed card ran at 25 MHz. Rates the
+	 * clock driver cannot double (the 400 kHz identification clock)
+	 * keep the old behaviour.
+	 */
+	ret = clk_set_rate(&priv->clk, freq * 2);
+	if (ret == freq * 2)
+		return freq;
+
 	ret = clk_set_rate(&priv->clk, freq);
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		debug("%s: err=%d\n", __func__, ret);
